        <article data-uid="GameFramework.StateMachine.GameStateMachine">
  
  
  <h1 id="GameFramework_StateMachine_GameStateMachine" data-uid="GameFramework.StateMachine.GameStateMachine" class="text-break">
    Class GameStateMachine
    
  </h1>
  
  <div class="facts text-secondary">
    <dl><dt>Namespace</dt><dd><a class="xref" href="GameFramework.StateMachine.html">GameFramework.StateMachine</a></dd></dl>
    <dl><dt>Assembly</dt><dd>cs.temp.dll.dll</dd></dl>
  </div>
  
  <div class="markdown summary"><p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.StateMachine.GameStateMachine.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="2" sourceendlinenumber="3">Game State Machine manages game state transitions with proper event publishing
Ensures TimeService and other systems receive correct state change notifications</p>
<p sourcefile="api/GameFramework.StateMachine.GameStateMachine.yml" sourcestartlinenumber="5" sourceendlinenumber="7">Design: Uses dependency injection and factory pattern for state creation
Pros: Clean separation of concerns, proper event handling, extensible state creation
Cons: Requires all states to be registered in factory</p>
</div>
  <div class="markdown conceptual"></div>

  <div class="codewrapper">
    <pre><code class="lang-csharp hljs">public class GameStateMachine : IGameStateMachine</code></pre>
  </div>
  
  
  
  
